# Port the tst_test (new API) library off fork()/vfork()/mmap for wasm32.
#
# wasm has no fork()/vfork() and no MAP_SHARED memory. This ports every
# such use the curated syscall tests actually reach (dead uses compile
# via the force-included packages/ltp/wasm-compat.h and are dropped by
# wasm-ld's dead-code elimination):
#   * tst_test.c fork_testrun(): the one supervised test child becomes a
#     copy-clone (clone without CLONE_VM); its result counters -- no longer
#     in a shared page -- are handed back to the parent over a pipe.
#   * tst_test.c setup_ipc()/cleanup_ipc(): the MAP_SHARED results page
#     becomes a private heap allocation; checkpoints/child-reinit, which
#     need real shared memory, tst_brk(TCONF).
#   * tst_test.c SAFE_FORK(): stubbed to tst_brk(TCONF); a test forking its
#     own children cannot be expressed by a fresh-stack callback clone.
#   * tst_tmpdir.c tst_rmdir(): drops the msync/munmap of the never-mapped
#     checkpoint futex page.
#   * tst_buffers.c: guarded buffers lose their mmap'd PROT_NONE guard page
#     and become plain heap allocations (the canary check still runs).
#   * tst_cmd.c: the command runner's vfork()+exec becomes a copy-clone.
